Subject: [PATCH next 0053] thunderbolt: stream: transactional HopID ownership

A stream device kept requested and owned HopIDs in the same fields:
attach ignored allocation failures and left the requested IDs there,
so an open could enable paths on HopIDs the device never allocated and
detach/release then freed IDs that belonged to someone else. Replacing
an ID released the old one before the new one was allocated, so a
failed write left a released ID behind, and writing the ID the device
already owned allocated it a second time and failed.

Track ownership per direction (in_owned/out_owned). Acquire before
release on every replacement and roll back a failed property update,
treat a write of the owned ID as a no-op, publish and release only owned
IDs, hand them to the retained GPU context when its paths are still
pending, and refuse an open without owned IDs. Insert a new device into
the group list and attach it under one sg->lock (the probe walks the list
under that lock), make attach idempotent, and deregister the misc device
only if it was registered.

No data-path change.

